INT. SAFE HOUSE - WAREHOUSE LOFT - NIGHT

A raw concrete loft above a shuttered print shop. Plastic sheeting over broken windows. A table with a laptop, four phones, and an open pizza box. A single lamp. Rain hammers the tin roof.

FIVE PEOPLE sit around the table. The mood is brittle.

DOMINIKA SZCZEPAŃSKA-REYES (40s, team leader, silver streak in black hair) paces the room with a phone against her chest.

OTIS WHITLOW (50s, tech, cardigan over body armour) stares at the laptop screen.

KALINDA RAINEY (30s, field agent, torn jacket, bandaged hand) sits on the table's edge, swinging a boot.

TEODOR VASILESCU (30s, driver, nervous, cigarette cupped in his palm) keeps checking the window.

And in the corner on a wooden chair, hands zip-tied behind him, sits MAXIMILLIAN HOLT (60s, tailored suit, torn at the knees). His face is calm, as if he were waiting for a train.

DOMINIKA
Otis. How long?

OTIS
Four minutes. Maybe five.

DOMINIKA
Maybe?

OTIS
The uplink's unstable.

KALINDA
They'll be here before it finishes.

OTIS
They won't.

KALINDA
They will.

TEODOR
(from window)
Headlights. Two blocks.

DOMINIKA
Whose?

TEODOR
Don't know.

DOMINIKA
Teodor, whose?

TEODOR
I can't see! The rain!

Dominika crosses to the window in three strides. Teodor makes room. She presses her forehead to the glass. A pair of white lights crawls along the wet street. Stops. Cuts out.

DOMINIKA
Parked.

KALINDA
They're early.

DOMINIKA
They're patient.

MAXIMILLIAN
(from corner, mild)
They're my friends.

All heads turn. He gives a small, pleasant smile.

MAXIMILLIAN (CONT'D)
They've been very patient with me. Longer than you, Dominika.

DOMINIKA
Shut him up.

KALINDA
With what?

DOMINIKA
Anything.

Kalinda rummages in her jacket. Finds a roll of tape. Strides across the loft, tears a strip, and presses it over his mouth. His smile continues beneath the tape, visible in the eyes.

OTIS
Three minutes.

TEODOR
Boss, what do we do if it's them?

DOMINIKA
We don't open.

TEODOR
They'll break the door.

DOMINIKA
Then we are not here.

KALINDA
We're very much here.

DOMINIKA
We are leaving.

OTIS
I can't leave. The transfer.

DOMINIKA
Then finish it. Kalinda, you're with Otis. Teodor, the van, engine on, lights off.

TEODOR
And him?

DOMINIKA
He comes.

TEODOR
Boss, he's a hostage. We take him out the back, they'll see.

DOMINIKA
He's not a hostage, Teodor. He's insurance.

On the chair, Maximilian's eyebrows lift.

KALINDA
(to Maximilian)
Don't look so pleased.

OTIS
Two minutes. I'm at ninety percent.

DOMINIKA
Where's the flash drive?

OTIS
In the pizza box.

DOMINIKA
You put it in the pizza box?

OTIS
They never look in the pizza box.

DOMINIKA
Otis!

OTIS
It's worked before!

She snatches the box. Flips the lid. Under the congealed cheese lies a thumb drive in a sandwich bag. She holds it up. A flicker of grim approval crosses her face.

DOMINIKA
Fine.

A thump on the stairs. Then another. Everyone freezes. Dominika puts her finger to her lips. Footsteps climb, slow, unhurried.

TEODOR
(whispering)
That's them.

KALINDA
(whispering)
That's one of them.

DOMINIKA
(whispering)
Otis.

OTIS
(whispering)
Ninety-eight.

The footsteps stop at the door. A polite knock. Three times.

Behind the tape, Maximilian closes his eyes, relieved.

Dominika raises her pistol and aims at the door.

DOMINIKA
(whispering)
Teodor. Back stairs.

TEODOR
Boss...

DOMINIKA
Go.

FADE OUT.
